.SH "DAEMON COORDINATION"
When run in full mode (no parity flag), zshrs cooperates with a
singleton coordinator process,
.BR zshrs-daemon ,
addressed via
.IR ~/.zshrs/daemon.sock .
The daemon owns ALL mutation:
.IP \fBfsnotify\fR 8
watches
.IR ~/.zshrc ,
.BR $fpath ,
plugin trees; invalidates affected cache shards on change.
.IP \fBcompile\fR 8
rkyv image writes for script_cache, plugin_cache, autoload_cache,
catalog.db rebuilds, log rotation, integrity scans.
.IP "\fBIPC routing\fR" 8
cross-shell pub/sub
.RB ( zsubscribe ,
.BR znotify ,
.BR zsend ,
.BR ztag ),
shell registry
.RB ( zls ,
.BR zid ,
.BR zping ),
and the session-persistent job supervisor
.RB ( zjob ,
planned).
.PP
100+ thin
.B zshrs
clients (e.g. one per tmux pane) mmap the daemon's outputs directly
for hot lookups (zero IPC) and use the socket only for control-plane
events (rebuild, fpath_changed, stats_flush, cross-shell dispatch).
Clients spawn zero background threads, polling timers, or SQLite
handles. See
.BR zd (1)
for daemon administration.
.PP
.B POSIX mode never spawns the daemon.
.SH "AHEAD-OF-TIME COMPILATION"
The
.B zbuild
builtin turns one or more scripts into a standalone executable:
.B zbuild \-\-in
.I script.zsh ...
.B \-\-out
.IR app .
By default it appends the zstd\-compressed script source to a copy of the
running
.B zshrs
binary. At launch the embedded scripts run in input order as one program, so
a single file ships and no zsh or zshrs install is needed; the scripts are
still parsed and compiled at startup.
.PP
With
.B \-\-native
the scripts are compiled to a
.B fusevm
chunk, lowered to native machine code with Cranelift, and linked against
.B libzsh.a
into a standalone binary. The program's control flow is native; each shell
operation calls into the linked zsh runtime.
.PP
AOT and the daily\-driver cache are two separate tracks: AOT for deploy
binaries; the rkyv cache for the interactive shell.
.SH "ASPECT-ORIENTED INTERCEPTS"
.B zshrs
supports
.BR before ,
.BR after ,
and
.B around
advice on every command, builtin, and user function. Advice is
registered via the
.B intercepts
crate (see
.IR src/intercepts/ )
and runs in-process inside fusevm \(em no
.BR fork (2)
\(em which makes it cheap enough for production tracing, profiling,
auditing, or per-command behaviour overlays. This is the foundation
for
.BR zpwrTrace ,
.BR zpwrFlame ,
.B zpwrTop
and the rest of the
.B zpwr
introspection stack.
.SH "WORKERS & NO-FORK ARCHITECTURE"
zshrs ships a persistent worker pool: long-lived processes that
service builtins, common externals
.RB ( ls ", " cat ", " grep ", "
etc., on the user's allowlist), and pipeline stages without invoking
.BR fork (2)
on every command. This is invisible to scripts: pipelines compose,
redirections work, job control behaves identically. Workers can be
disabled via
.B "setopt no_workers"
or by the parity flags.
.SH "RECORDER"
.B zshrs-recorder
.RI ( bins/zshrs-recorder.rs )
captures shell sessions as a structured event stream. Feature-gated;
see
.BR docs/RECORDER.md " and " docs/RECORDER_PROTOCOL.md
for the on-disk schema. The replay surface
.RB ( zpwrReplay )
sits on top of it.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
Standard zsh-recognised variables (see SPECIAL PARAMETERS) plus
zshrs additions:
.TP
.B HELPDIR
Directory of \fBrun\-help\fR's help database. Unless already set, zshrs points it at
.IR ~/.zshrs/help ,
where the bundled copy is materialised (zsh's own \fBrun\-help\fR hardcodes the
help path of whichever zsh built it). A shell parameter only; never exported.
Not set under \fB\-\-zsh\fR.
.TP
.B MANPATH\fR, \fBINFOPATH
Extended with \fI~/.zshrs/man\fR and \fI~/.zshrs/info\fR plus an empty trailing
entry, so the bundled zsh and zshrs pages (\fBman zshall\fR, \fBman zshrsall\fR)
resolve without hiding the system's own. Not set under \fB\-\-zsh\fR.
.TP
.B ZSHRS_HOME
Override the state root (caches, databases, logs, daemon socket). Default:
.IR ~/.zshrs/ .
.TP
.B ZSHRS_CACHE
Set to \fB0\fR to disable the caches and the daemon. The parity modes
(\fB\-\-zsh\fR, \fB\-\-bash\fR, \fB\-\-ksh\fR, \fB\-\-sh\fR, \fB\-\-csh\fR, \fB\-\-posix\fR) set it.
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LOG
.BR tracing -style filter for the structured log. Examples:
.BR debug ", " "zshrs::ported::lex=trace" ", " "zshrs=info,fusevm=trace" .
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LONG_CMD_PRE_THRESHOLD
Seconds. Commands taking longer fire the preexec long-cmd hook.
.TP
.B ZSHRS_NO_DAEMON
Suppress daemon connection (per-invocation override of full mode).
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Key for the
.B ai
builtin's default provider (the variable named by
.BR [ai]\ api_key_env ).
.TP
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ", " GOOGLE_API_KEY ", " GEMINI_API_KEY
Keys for
.B ai \-P openai
and
.BR "ai \-P gemini" .
.TP
.BR ZSHRS_AI_BASE_URL ", " ZSHRS_AI_LOCAL_KEY
Endpoint and key for
.B ai \-P local
(an OpenAI-compatible server; default endpoint
.IR http://localhost:1234/v1/chat/completions ).
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Endpoint for
.B ai \-P ollama
(default
.IR http://localhost:11434 ).
.TP
.B ZSHRS_AI_MODE
.B mock-only
makes an
.B ai
prompt that no
.B \-M
mock matches an error instead of a live call.
.SH "FILES"
.TP
.I ~/.zshrs/
State root (\fBZSHRS_HOME\fR). Holds the rkyv caches
.RB ( autoloads.rkyv ,
.BR scripts.rkyv ,
.BR deparse.rkyv ),
the SQLite databases
.RB ( catalog.db ,
.BR history.db ,
.BR plugins.db ,
.BR compsys.db ),
the daemon files
.BR daemon.sock " and " daemon.pid ,
the logs
.RB ( zshrs.log ,
.BR zshrs-daemon.log ),
and the configuration files
.RB ( zshrs.toml ,
.BR zshrs-daemon.toml ,
.BR zshrs-recorder.toml ).
.TP
.I ~/.zshrs/zshrs-daemon.toml
Optional daemon config; see
.BR zd (1).
.TP
.I ~/.zshenv,\ ~/.zprofile,\ ~/.zshrc,\ ~/.zlogin,\ ~/.zlogout
Standard zsh startup files (used identically to upstream zsh).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Identical to
.BR zsh (1):
the shell exits with the status of the last command or with
.B $?
at the time of an
.B exit
call. 127 indicates command-not-found; 126 indicates a permission
error. Trap handlers and
.B zshexit
fire before the actual exit syscall.
.SH "COMPATIBILITY GUARANTEES"
.B zshrs
treats the zsh upstream
.B C
source under
.IR src/zsh/Src/
as the spec floor. Bytecode and SQLite formats are versioned and
migration-safe; old caches either upgrade cleanly or rebuild
silently. A
.IR .zshrc " " "that worked yesterday"
must work today. Compat-floor regressions against
.BR zpwr ,
.BR zsh-more-completions ,
.BR oh-my-zsh ,
.BR zinit ,
.BR p10k ,
and the standard plugin set are catastrophic; the parity test corpus
.RB ( tests/zsh_compat_parity_gaps.rs ,
20,000+ cases) is gating.
.PP
.B Architectural invariants:
.IP "" 4
.B tree_walker_absent
\(em the C-style AST walker is unreachable from any code path.
fusevm bytecode is the only executor.
.IP "" 4
.B no_tree_walker_dispatch
\(em no Rust call-site re-introduces an
.BR execlist / execpline / execcmd
shape; pinned by tests.
.IP "" 4
.B port_purity
\(em every
.B pub fn
under
.B src/ported/
maps to a real
.B Src/x.c
function name (allowlist in
.BR tests/data/fake_fn_allowlist.txt ).
.IP "" 4
.B file_mapping
\(em ports live in the Rust file matching their C basename
(allowlist in
.BR tests/data/ported_fn_file_mapping_allowlist.txt ).
.SH "DIAGNOSTICS"
Errors take the form
.BI "zshrs: " command ": " reason
on stderr. Informational chatter (init, indexing, autoload pre-warm,
plugin compile) goes to
.IR ~/.zshrs/zshrs.log
via
.BR tracing ;
it is never printed to the terminal. No startup banner. No deprecation
nags. No spell-correction prompts. No "did you mean" hints. No
tip-of-the-day. No "use \fB\-\-help\fR for more" suffix in error
messages.
.SH "DEBUGGING & INTROSPECTION"
.TP
.B \-\-disasm
Print fusevm opcodes before VM execution.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-tokens
Token stream from lex.rs.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-ast
Parsed AST from parse.rs.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-wordcode
zsh-style wordcode (for parity comparison against
.BR zcompile ).
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-zwc
Inspect a
.B *.zwc
bytecode bundle.
.TP
.B \-\-tiers
Run a script, then report which fusevm execution tier took each of its
chunks \(em and for the chunks that reached neither, which op kinds kept
them out. The answer comes from fusevm's own eligibility and cache
predicates, so it is the compiler's account rather than an estimate.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-reflection
JSON self-description of every builtin, keyword and option.
.B \-\-dump\-reference\-html
emits the same corpus as HTML;
.B \-\-names
lists every canonical name, one per line.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-plugins
JSON for every plugin the most recent recorded session sourced or put on fpath, grouped by the manager that installed it.
The daemon writes the list to \fIplugins.db\fR when it ingests a recorder shard; the output is empty until one has been ingested.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Full diagnostic report; useful when filing issues.
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LOG
.BR tracing -style filter on the structured log.
